      "response": "{\"causal_chain\": \"AI commoditizes execution (content, code, analysis) → value migrates from 'doing' to 'orchestrating workflows' and 'owning distribution' → capital flows concentrate into AI infrastructure ($4.2T by 2035) and AI-enabled services → bottleneck shifts from skill to DISTRIBUTION + TRUST + DATA LOOPS. The real value creation happens not where AI is built but where AI meets a specific vertical's messy reality (localization, compliance, cultural context). Vietnamese founder sits at the intersection of low-cost labor arbitrage (still real for 3-5 more years) AND Southeast Asian digital economy growth (Internet economy $218B→$600B+ by 2030). The mechanism: AI deflates the cost of producing anything digital → whoever owns the customer relationship and distribution channel captures the margin that used to go to producers.\", \"contradictions\": [\"Andrew Ng says AI only pays off for large companies [?|0.47] vs AI Wealth Builders showing small tools became products [T|0.63] — RESOLUTION: Ng refers to training foundation models; the wealth creation happens in APPLYING AI to specific workflows. Small founders win at application layer, not infrastructure. This is the critical distinction.\", \"VC all going to AI [T|0.63] vs $500 founder capital — RESOLUTION: VC money flows into AI infrastructure, creating FREE/CHEAP tools that $500 founders can weaponize. The VC subsidy is the founder's advantage. Every dollar Anthropic/OpenAI burns on compute becomes a capability the founder gets for $20/month.\", \"Intangible assets + AI create value [T|0.68] vs empty operator_intelligence and cash_flow_mechanics dimensions — RESOLUTION: Research captured the macro thesis but missed the ground-level HOW. The gap between macro AI narrative and actual cashflow mechanics is where most founders fail. Intelligence without execution path = zero.\"], \"inferred_gaps\": [\"[INFERRED] Vietnam's specific regulatory environment creates arbitrage: VN businesses can serve global markets with minimal regulatory overhead vs EU/US compliance costs. Data privacy laws less restrictive = faster iteration.\", \"[INFERRED] The 15-Technique SPLIT showing optimism_bias + blind_spot detected means the research over-indexed on AI opportunity and under-indexed on execution barriers. The blind spot is likely: how does a $500 founder actually GET CUSTOMERS, not how do they build products.\", \"[INFERRED] Missing cash_flow_mechanics dimension is the most dangerous gap. Without understanding actual payment flows, commission structures, and collection cycles in Vietnam, any model is theoretical.\", \"[INFERRED] Cross-border payment infrastructure (Wise, Payoneer, Stripe Atlas) has matured enough that VN founders can collect global revenue, but withdrawal fees (1-3%) and forex spread eat into thin margins.\"]}"
