    "step_5_verdict": {
      "response": "{\"verdict\": \"GO\", \"top_3\": [{\"rank\": 1, \"model\": \"4. AI Workflow Automation Consultant\", \"why\": \"Fastest to revenue with highest 10-year durability. VN market is 3-5 years behind in AI adoption — you are riding a wave that has not yet arrived. Every engagement teaches you more. Zero startup cost. The demand is latent but massive: VN has 800K+ SMBs that still run on Excel and Zalo. Month-1 action is clear and testable. This model also FEEDS models 2, 6, and 9 — every automation client reveals SaaS gaps, localization needs, and lead gen opportunities.\"}, {\"rank\": 2, \"model\": \"9. B2B Lead Generation Service\", \"why\": \"Second fastest to recurring revenue. VN export companies desperately need international clients but have zero outreach capability. AI tools make you a one-person lead gen machine. This model builds the DISTRIBUTION ASSET that makes every other model more valuable — if you can generate leads for clients, you can generate leads for yourself. Start this in parallel with model 4 — same skill set, different packaging.\"}, {\"rank\": 3, \"model\": \"7. Deal Flow Aggregator\", \"why\": \"Zero cost, pure effort. Connects you to the LARGEST money flows in Vietnam (real estate, business transfers). The information asymmetry in VN deal markets is staggering — being the organized information node in a chaotic market is a structural advantage. This model has the highest upside variance: one $500K deal referral at 1% = $5K from a single introduction. Start passively alongside models 4 and 9.\"}], \"key_insight\": \"The research shows optimism_bias toward AI macro trends but the founder's actual advantage is not AI itself — it is being the HUMAN BRIDGE between AI capabilities and Vietnamese market reality. AI tools are commoditized and free. What is scarce is someone who understands both the tools AND the local context: Vietnamese business culture, regulatory environment, payment systems, and trust networks. The winning strategy is not 'build AI products' but 'be the person who makes AI work in Vietnam.' This is a 10+ year advantage because cultural context is the one thing AI cannot automate, and Vietnam's complexity (language, regulations, business customs) creates a natural moat against foreign competitors.\", \"asymmetric_play\": \"Model 4 (AI Workflow Automation) has massive asymmetry: downside is $0 lost and 90 days of learning time (which has value regardless). Upside is positioning yourself as THE AI automation expert in VN market of 800K+ SMBs before the adoption wave hits. If VN follows the same adoption curve as Thailand and Indonesia (2-3 year lag), you have a 2-year head start to build templates, reputation, and client base before competition arrives. The 10x scenario: you become the go-to AI implementation partner for VN subsidiaries of multinational companies (Samsung, Intel, LG all have major VN operations), charging $5-20K per engagement instead of $500-1K.\", \"kill_go_reasoning\": \"GO because: (1) All 10 models are viable at $0-500 startup cost, (2) The founder's geographic position in Vietnam is a STRUCTURAL advantage for 7 of 10 models, not a disadvantage, (3) AI tool commoditization means the founder gets enterprise-grade capabilities at consumer prices, (4) Vietnam's economic growth trajectory (GDP growth 6-7% annually, digital economy tripling by 2030) provides a rising tide, (5) The portfolio approach — start 3 models simultaneously, double down on whichever gets traction first — reduces single-point-of-failure risk to near zero. The only scenario where this fails is if the founder does not execute consistently for 90+ days. The constraint is discipline, not capital or market.\"}"
